A||||9||Greg Piet||Factory Wing deal||||1||
Z||000000||Greg Piet||01-28-2000||05:12 PM||||Well I blew my motor in my 85 SE, so a local fiero guy is replacing it for me.  <BR>His wife screwed up the front end of her fiero and they are not going to fix it.  So the mechanic offered me her rear decklid and wing and instalation for $150 which is in great shape and the color matches. <BR>After a little thinking I called him and said "DO IT".  I think that is a good deal, and the cost to do the motor was really fair.  Hopefully all will be well when I get it back, and I'll have a wing too!||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||01-28-2000||07:47 PM||||even if you don't install them now, get the springs for that deck lid as well. the wing lid has heavier springs.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||01-28-2000||08:18 PM||||Anybody tried the gas shocks for the deck lid instead of the stock springs?  I forget who sells them, but it seemed like a good idea.||||reg||1
Z||000003||pherder||01-28-2000||08:30 PM||||Monkeyman,<P>Rodney Dickman sells them and they are beautiful! <P>You can get either 1 or 2 depending on your wishes.<P>Paul||||reg||4
Z||000004||TOM||01-28-2000||08:43 PM||||I am not saying anything about rodney personnaly. He is on our side but I think the gas struts are just more clutter that is not needed if you use the right springs||||reg||1
Z||000005||fiero56||01-28-2000||09:17 PM||||I saw a set of Rodney's gas springs installed on a Northstat conversion at Columbus. I like the look, but everyone has their own taste.||||reg||1
